<title>CHINA: HK's Dragonair suspends service to Phnom Penh.</title>
<headline>HK's Dragonair suspends service to Phnom Penh.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong Dragon Airlines Ltd said on Tuesday it has supended its twice weekly service between Hong Kong and Phnom Penh in Cambodia due to the closure of Phnom Penh's Pochentong Airport.</p>
<p>Dragonair said flights KA200 from Hong Kong to Phom Penh and KA201 from Phnom Pehn to Hong Kong which operate on Tuesdays and Saturdays have been temporily suspended.</p>
<p>The services will resume when the airport reopens and the airline is completely satisfied it is safe to do so, Dragonair said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6441</p>
</text>
